%N A398629 Numbers that can be obtained by removing the first and last digits of a square.
%C A398629 Leading 0s are disallowed, so 16 is excluded even though 142^2 = 20164, for example.
%H A398629 Eric Fox, <a href="/A398629/b398629.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A398629 371 is in this sequence: 154^2 = 23716.
%e A398629 880 is in this sequence: 197^2 = 38809, 298^2 = 88804.
%t A398629 filter[n_] := IntegerDigits[n^2][[2 ;; -2]] /. {0 .., __} :> Nothing; Union[FromDigits /@ filter /@ Range[10, 331]] (* _Alexander Krivilev_, Oct 01 2026 *)
%o A398629 (PARI) isok(k) = #select(issquare, setbinop((x,y)->eval(concat(Str(x), concat(Str(k), Str(y)))), [1..9], [0..9])); \\ _Michel Marcus_, Oct 04 2026
